Don''t narrate "the ticket won''t persist until committed" on every ticket edit. Either quietly fold the bookkeeping into a commit or trust the normal commit flow.', 'done', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-06 08:48:11', '2026-06-06 08:48:16', NULL, 'c5b9117bb4006a022fb4a442abf372d1', 1) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_id=excluded.parent_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at > tickets.updated_at OR (excluded.updated_at = tickets.updated_at AND excluded.hash > tickets.hash);
INSERT INTO tickets (id, type, parent_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('T-54', 'task', NULL, 'Surface ticket-ID collisions loudly at changelog replay', 'Ticket IDs are allocated as max(existing)+1 against the *local* changelog, so two clones/branches/sessions that file between syncs can both pick the same T-NNN. This is an accepted cost of sequential IDs with no central authority (git provisions none) — we don''t want to prevent it.

The real hazard is that it''s currently *silent*: `tickets` replays with `ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE`, so two unrelated tickets claiming one id merge into a single row (higher updated_at/hash wins) with no error. The corruption is invisible until someone notices a wrong title.

Make it loud instead of preventing it: at changelog replay / `pql plan rebuild`, detect when one `id` is claimed by two distinct `hash` lineages (different created_at/title for the same id) and surface it as a diagnostic rather than letting the upsert paper over it. Keeps sequential human-readable IDs; turns invisible merge into a rebuild-time warning the maintainer can reconcile by re-filing one under a fresh id.

Context: hit live on 2026-06-06 — local T-52 collided with an already-pushed remote T-52, resolved by re-filing as T-53.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-06 08:53:46', '2026-06-06 08:53:46', NULL, '17d9e77f443a6fe26e19d075873a5031', 1) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_id=excluded.parent_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at > tickets.updated_at OR (excluded.updated_at = tickets.updated_at AND excluded.hash > tickets.hash);
